# Parent & Me activities

## Core rule

> **Use Parent & Me when the grown-up and little one are doing the experience together.**

A parent seeing **Parent & Me** should understand: *we do this together — not just an activity I take my child to.*

The caregiver participates—not supervising from the side, not using separate childcare while the adult does something else.

## Include when

- Intentionally designed for caregiver + child together
- Caregiver participation is expected or central (parent + baby yoga, stroller fitness, parent-child art/music, family yoga, caregiver-baby groups)
- Ages 0–5 appropriate; meaningful shared experience

## Do not use Parent & Me when

- Adult activity with on-site childcare → future **Childcare available** attribute (not this type)
- Kids class where parents wait nearby / merely stay
- Standard storytime / library program (use **Stories** even if caregivers attend)
- Toddler gymnastics / playground where adults happen to be present
- Child is only allowed to accompany the caregiver
- Primary fit is clearly **Music & Movement**, **Arts & Crafts**, etc. — use that type instead when it’s a better primary label

## Parent & Me vs Childcare available

| Concept | Need |
|---------|------|
| **Parent & Me** | We do it together |
| **Childcare available** *(future attribute)* | Something for me, with care for them |

Do not collapse these into one type.

## Series vs one-off

Multi-week enrollment (e.g. Music Together semester) = **one series row**, not weekly event spam. Drop-in weekly sessions that are independently attendable may stay dated.

Do not put exact open seats or waitlisted times in public **Good to know** — link to the provider for current availability. See `class-series-availability.mdc`.

## Naming

Activity type label: **Parent & Me** (not “Grown-up + Me”). Supporting copy may say “for little ones and their grown-ups.”

**Parent & Me** is in the Activity Type filter.

